window.products.push({"id":176966,"name":"Banneton Proofing Basket for Bread Rising – 10” Large Proofing Basket Bowl for Starter Sourdough, Extra Sticky Dough | Comes with Linen Cloth Liner | ","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71saKEd8gUL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Ever dream of taking 1st Place in the county fair for “Best White Bread?” Wish you could make a legendary rye loaf that’s the envy of the neighborhood? Looking for a sourdough proofing basket to tackle that world-famous Tartine bread recipe? At PNW Kitchen , it’s our mission to arm you with premium-quality bread baking supplies so you can make gourmet bread right at home. Q: What is the proofing cloth used for? A: The basket liner is excellent for making your dough wetter so your bread comes out nice and fluffy. It’s also great for beginners who are just learning! Q: What’s the best type of flour to use? A: Rice flour is by far the best flour for your banneton proofing basket. Its fantastic stickiness-reducing properties allow the dough to slip right out while also maintaining optimal proofing. How to Use Your Cane Proofing Basket 1. Generously flour the basket (or liner, if you’re using one)–we highly recommend using rice flour for best results. Make sure to get your flour in the nooks and crannies, too!2. Place kneaded dough inside the basket and allow dough to rise.3. Transfer your dough onto a baking sheet and place in the oven (do NOT place the basket in the oven). Bake the loaf according to your desired recipe. How to Clean Your Bread Making Kit To clean the basket, simply take a dough scraper or bread scraper and brush out the leftover flour. It’s that easy!To clean the liner, just tap out any excess flour and it’s ready to reuse. Alternatively, you can soak the liner in cool water and let air dry. Who It’s For Both casual home bakers and professionals Bread lovers  People getting serious about making bread Thoughtful gift givers Don’t spend another minute slaving over mediocre bread. Get your proofing basket now and start enjoying great-looking and tasting bread for years to come!","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71saKEd8gUL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PNW Kitchen","source_asin":"B07D6H4NBM","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-176966","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07D6H4NBM","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B07D6H4NBM","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
window.products.push({"id":176967,"name":"Oudh Nasaem 60gm | 1 Pack | Bakhoor بخور | Beautiful Ever-Lasting Fragrance Evoking Aroma from The East | by Nabeel Perfumes","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":15.65,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71XZMTlYTGL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Bakhoor or Bakhur, an Arabic word which means Fumes, is endlessly known for performing houses or environmental factors. The term Bakhoor in this sense fundamentally alludes to the wood chips that are absorbed fragrant Oud oils; which is the oil separated from the uncommon Aquilaria tree. An irresistible kind of shape takes a hold of the heartwood of the tree and later on, produces a dim fragrant sap that delivers the oil. How to Use: Take a piece of burning charcoal and heat a corner of it with a small flame(lighter/ cooker) for about 60 seconds until it becomes red hot. Place the piece of coal in incense burner Sit back as the beautiful fragrance fills the room Bakhoor is used during special occasions such as weddings, or simply for relaxing purposes. In Arabian culture, it’s a traditional gesture to pass bakhoor among guests, so they can scent their hair, clothing and hands. This is believed to be a as integral to hospitality as serving coffee and dates.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71XZMTlYTGL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"NABEEL","source_asin":"B09122HT2P","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-176967","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09122HT2P","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B09122HT2P","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
